# Environments
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# Data — raw PDFs and intermediate parse output are not committed.
#
# PLAN.md Phase 19 wants a fresh machine to start without re-ingesting
# seven PDFs. That needs only the SERVING artifacts: the S1 chunks the MVP
# index is built from, plus the Chunk Store (~28MB total). The other six
# benchmark configs are ~71MB of experiment output, fully regenerable with
# `python scripts/chunk.py --all-benchmark`, so they stay out — a 100MB
# repo of regenerable artifacts is a real cost (clone time, GitHub's 100MB
# per-file limit) for no recovery benefit.
data/raw/*.pdf
data/parsed/
data/cleaned/

# The original download folder — a redundant copy of the same seven PDFs
# already staged into data/raw/ with SHA-256 checksums. ~48MB of
# copyrighted WHO/USPSTF source documents that should not live in the
# repository at all (data/raw/CHECKSUMS.sha256 is what pins the corpus;
# docs/knowledge-base.md records provenance and licensing).
WHO-ICRC Basic Emergency Care (2)/
*.pdf
data/chunks/1.0_A.jsonl
data/chunks/1.0_B.jsonl
data/chunks/benchmark/*.jsonl
!data/chunks/benchmark/1.0_S1.jsonl

# App storage
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

